 "note": "Completed-season records, used as the prior a small in-season sample is shrunk toward.\n\nTHE BIAS THIS FILE CAN CAUSE, stated plainly because it already happened: the first version held six players and every one of them was an attacker. That does not merely leave defenders uncovered — it actively disadvantages them, because a covered player gets a stable two-season signal while an uncovered one is left with a one-gameweek sample. The app duly recommended selling Gabriel, the highest-scoring defender in the game last season on 209 points, while keeping a striker who had blanked. A partial prior is not a neutral prior.\n\nSo coverage is now checked, not assumed: `history.coverage()` reports players per position and a test fails if any position is thin. Fixing the numbers without fixing the check would leave the same trap set for next time.\n\n`appearances_estimated: true` marks a season where the published source gave total points but not appearances. The estimate used is a FULL 38-game season, deliberately the maximum, so points-per-appearance comes out as a floor rather than a guess upward — an unsourced figure can only understate a player here, never inflate one. `scripts/fetch_history.py` replaces the whole file with exact official numbers from the FPL API, which carries appearances directly.",
